Z||000000||Ferrari_cdn||09-23-2001||01:52 AM||||I notice in my garage when I play with the shifter, I can see the reverse light come on very early when shifting into reverse (4 spd).  It means when I'm just about to leave the notch for the 1st and into reverse it'll come on but when I am shifting into first, I can STILL turn on the reverse light if I am pushing the stick up, but a little to the left.  Meaning reverse lights CAN be on if I keep the shifter a bit to the left when driving and still be in first.<P>When I shift from 3rd or 4th to 1st, I guess I blink the reverse lights momentarily a few times.  When I followed my father in his car when he drove my car, I see the white lights blink on and off quickly often.<P>Is there a way I can change the switch so that it'll come on when I'm all the way to the left and IN the reverse gear?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ferrari_2.JPG">   <BR>'84 2m4, 4 speed, 106k miles (157k km)  AIM: CanadianFiero<p>[This message has been edited by Ferrari_cdn (edited 09-23-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||JetroGT||09-23-2001||04:24 AM||||It's a good tail gater deturent!||||reg||10
Z||000002||rogergarrison||09-23-2001||12:39 PM||||just what I was thinking. Even a override switch would be cool, Sure would get tailgaters attention.<P>European models of my car have a seperate back up lite as an option, mounted under the bumper and look like fog lites. Only US versions have the back up lite in the turn lenses. Ive thought about putting some foglites there aimed so they hit tailgaters rite in the face.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 09-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||09-23-2001||12:48 PM||||Should be a little adjustment screw on the switch under the shift plate? The shifter is making contact before you are fully in reverse. Remove the shift knob & ash trays then the 4 screw under the astrays that hold the shift pod in place, you'll see the reverse switch to the left.<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||4
